From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SoloLuck ops <releases@sololuck.io>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:53:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] SoloLuck: per-port difficulty floors, lifetime reject
 counters, donation address

Adds a serverdiff array to the config, one entry per serverurl. Each entry is
the minimum share difficulty for that port, enforced in two places: when a
client connects, the floor becomes its suggested difficulty (and its current
difficulty, if the start difficulty is lower); and a mining.suggest_difficulty
below the floor is raised to it. Neither path can take a client below the
floor of the port it connected on.

Adds diff-weighted lifetime reject counters per user and per worker to the
stats JSON, and logs the server a client authorised on.

Repoints donaddress from upstream's address to SoloLuck's. ckpool builds a
donation output only when "donation" in the config is at least 0.1, and
SoloLuck's pools run with it at 0, so no donation output is built and nothing
is paid to this address. In solo mode with no btcaddress configured, ckpool
also uses this address to check that it can build a coinbase; it is never
mined to.

Rebased onto ckpool v1.2.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
